A `{one,two}` brace group in a glob matches both files, and the glob view prints a file summary for each.
== args
input/{one,two}.md
== file input/one.md
---
description: First summary.
---
# one
== file input/two.md
---
description: Second summary.
---
# two
== stdout
glob view: input/{one,two}.md
input/one.md (4 lines): description: "First summary."
input/two.md (4 lines): description: "Second summary."
== stderr
== exit 0
